<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Nieuw-Amsterdam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1734–1747</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Nieuw-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a> is a pentagonal fortress built between 1734 and 1747 at the confluence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a> and Commewijne rivers, opposite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paramaribo">Paramaribo</a>. It was built after the French raids of the late seventeenth and early eighteenth centuries to defend the plantation colony of Suriname against attack from the sea. It later served as a prison and military post and is now an open-air museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-nieuw-amsterdam.jpg" alt="Fort Nieuw-Amsterdam" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jakob van der Schley · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AMH-6914-KB_Map_of_Nieuw_Amsterdam_fort.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
